# AgoraLume backend configuration.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (next to the executable) and edit it. Every line is
# optional — the defaults run a self-contained demo with simulated replies.
# Anything you set in your real shell environment overrides the file.
#
# LLM provider configuration (endpoint, key, tuning, pricing) is NOT here
# anymore — it lives in `llm.toml` under the data dir (see AGORALUME_DATA_DIR
# below), which the server creates on first run with every option commented
# out and explained. Edit that file directly, or use the Settings page in the
# running app; either takes effect without a restart. If you're upgrading from
# an older AgoraLume with AGORALUME_LLM* / AGORALUME_COMPRESS* set, the first
# run migrates them into llm.toml automatically and logs that it did — those
# variables are no longer read after that.

# --- Persistence ----------------------------------------------------------
# Save the workspace (personas/organizations/groups/settings) and chat logs to
# the data dir so they survive a restart. Defaults to on whenever llm.toml has
# `enabled = true` (a real run is worth keeping; a mock demo is throwaway).
# Set explicitly to force either way. llm.toml itself always persists
# regardless of this setting — losing a configured endpoint and key on a
# throwaway mock run would defeat the point of moving off environment
# variables.
#AGORALUME_PERSIST=1
# Data root (default ./data). llm.toml lives directly under this root,
# shared by every account; everything else (workspace.json, messages/,
# usage.json, ...) lives under accounts/<AGORALUME_ACCOUNT_ID>/. A pre-account
# install's flat files are migrated into accounts/<id>/ automatically, once,
# the first time the server starts against this data dir.
#AGORALUME_DATA_DIR=./data
# Which account this server process serves (default "default"). There's no
# login yet, so this is still a config-time choice, not something a client
# picks — see AGORALUME_DATA_DIR above.
#AGORALUME_ACCOUNT_ID=default

# --- Server ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Address to bind (default 127.0.0.1:8080). Use 0.0.0.0:<port> to expose on the
# LAN; the bundled exe serves the API and the site together on this one port.
# There's still no login for anyone who can reach that address — consider
# AGORALUME_CORS_ORIGINS below once this isn't just 127.0.0.1.
#AGORALUME_BIND=127.0.0.1:8080

# Open a browser on startup when serving the bundled site (default on).
# Set to 0 to skip.
#AGORALUME_OPEN=0

# Log verbosity (e.g. info, debug, agoralume_backend=debug).
#RUST_LOG=info

# Origins allowed to make cross-origin requests to the API, comma-separated.
# Default (unset): any origin — needed since the frontend's origin isn't
# fixed (a dev server on some port, or wherever the built site ends up
# hosted). If you *do* know your frontend's exact origin, setting this locks
# out every other origin's browser-side requests, including a PATCH to
# /llm/settings that only changes baseUrl to redirect where your stored API
# key gets sent — a real (if narrow) hardening step that needs no login
# system, since it's the browser itself refusing to send the request. Must
# match exactly (scheme + host + port, no trailing slash) or your own
# frontend gets locked out too. Unlike llm.toml, this needs a restart to
# take effect.
#AGORALUME_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,https://chat.example.com
